# Ansible Style Rules

## Task Names are Imperative Sentences
Every task must have a `name:` field. Names use present-tense imperative:
- CORRECT: `"Install nginx package"`
- CORRECT: `"Write nginx virtual host configuration"`
- CORRECT: `"Enable and start nginx service"`
- WRONG: `"nginx"` (noun only)
- WRONG: `"Installing nginx"` (gerund)
- WRONG: `"nginx package installation"` (passive noun phrase)

## YAML Formatting
- 2-space indent. No tabs ever.
- No trailing whitespace.
- Single blank line between top-level tasks.
- `ansible-lint` (default profile) enforces all of the above — run it in pre-commit hooks.

## Fully Qualified Collection Names (FQCN)
Always use FQCN. This is enforced by `ansible-lint` default profile:
```yaml
# CORRECT
ansible.builtin.package:
ansible.builtin.template:
ansible.builtin.service:
ansible.builtin.copy:
ansible.builtin.file:
ansible.builtin.user:
ansible.builtin.group:
ansible.builtin.command:
ansible.builtin.shell:
ansible.builtin.assert:
ansible.builtin.uri:
ansible.builtin.service_facts:

# WRONG
package:
template:
service:
```

## no_log for Sensitive Tasks
Add `no_log: true` to tasks that handle secrets. Prevents values from appearing in logs:
```yaml
- name: Create application user with password
  ansible.builtin.user:
    name: "{{ app_user }}"
    password: "{{ app_user_password | password_hash('sha512') }}"
  no_log: true

- name: Call API with auth token
  ansible.builtin.uri:
    url: "{{ api_endpoint }}"
    headers:
      Authorization: "Bearer {{ api_token }}"
  no_log: true
```

## loop over with_items
Use modern `loop:` syntax. `with_items:` is legacy and deprecated:
```yaml
# CORRECT
- name: Install required packages
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: "{{ item }}"
    state: present
  loop: "{{ nginx_packages }}"

# WRONG (legacy)
- name: Install required packages
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: "{{ item }}"
  with_items: "{{ nginx_packages }}"
```

## Variable Naming Convention
All role variables use `{rolename}_` prefix to avoid collisions across roles:
```yaml
# In roles/nginx/defaults/main.yml
nginx_port: 80
nginx_worker_processes: auto
nginx_worker_connections: 1024
nginx_server_name: "_"
nginx_document_root: /var/www/html
nginx_package_name: nginx
nginx_service_name: nginx
nginx_config_path: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
```
Never use unprefixed variable names like `port`, `workers`, `config_path` in role defaults.
